ive.", "watch": "If additional independent polling confirms the tied October survey, or if Democratic outside spending enters a race that so far has none, this could shift toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Flood (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Mike Flood is seeking a third full term in Nebraska's 1st District, a seat with a six-point Republican lean. Democrat Chris Backemeyer has run a competitive campaign, raising over $1.1 million, though Flood has out-raised him by more than two to one and holds a large cash advantage. No outside spending has materialized on either side.\n\nMost expert ratings place the race at Likely Republican, with a couple of outlets calling it Lean Republican. A late October poll from a Democratic-sponsored pollster showed the candidates essentially tied at 45 to 46 percent, a notable improvement for Backemeyer compared with spring surveys. Prediction markets still give Flood roughly a four-in-five chance of winning, reflecting the district's underlying Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1466, "margin": -6.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1237, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1206, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2177, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1689, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1777, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2315, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1394, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1156, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.114, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1142, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1121, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.173, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1374, "margin": -6.6}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1133, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "